# The scf_he_hf deck run on two MPI ranks -- same physics, same numbers.
#
# Nothing in the deck selects MPI; the rank count lives in run.sh. This case
# exists to check that the distributed path reproduces the serial energy, and to
# show the thread budget: with nranks > 1 each rank also spawns a MADNESS comm
# thread, and the MPI implementation usually wants a core for its own progress
# thread, so MAD_NUM_THREADS is workers *per rank*, not a total.
#
# This case needs >= 16 hwthreads (check.json gates on it, so smaller machines
# SKIP rather than fail). 2 ranks x (3 workers + 1 comm) is 8 MADNESS threads and
# the MPI progress threads need room beyond that: on an 8-core machine the run
# oversubscribes and does not finish -- 7 s on a 96-core node became a timeout on
# an 8-core laptop.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh                    (2 ranks x 3 workers)
#        NP=4 MAD_NUM_THREADS=2 ./run.sh

dft
    xc       hf
    maxiter  10
    econv    1e-4
    dconv    1e-3
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    He  0.0  0.0  0.0
end
